      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.2, & \\,y=1 \\\\ 0.8, & \\,y=3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=5]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,5)$ is shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=5] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,5) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =2.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
